course: dictionary
lesson: 9647
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One short word can have many meanings. «Sub» is a good example. Look at the words around it to find out which meaning the writer wants. «Subs often change games, and many matches are won by players coming off the bench.» Here the words games, matches and bench tell you that a sub is a player who comes on to replace another.
explain: Sometimes «sub» is a short form of a longer word. Ask: what would fit here? Then try the longer word in the sentence. If «substitute» makes sense, the sub means a substitute. In a sandwich shop, «sub» means a long sandwich, and in a school in America it can mean a substitute teacher.
explain: Many words have a prefix at the start. The prefix «sub-» means under or below. If you know this, you can work out the meaning of new words. A submarine goes under the water. A subway runs under the ground. Subtract means to take away, and it works by taking a number down.
fact: Many words have more than one meaning, so check the context.
fact: In sport, a sub is a substitute, a player who comes on to replace another.
fact: In North America, a sub is a long sandwich, also called a submarine sandwich.
fact: The prefix «sub-» means under or below, as in «submarine», «subway» and «subtract».
fact: The prefix «pre-» means before, as in «preview» and «prehistoric». Compare it with «sub-» to remember both.
exercise: «Subs often change games, and many matches are won by players coming off the bench.» In this sentence, what is a sub? | A teacher who fills in for a day | A long sandwich | A kind of boat that travels under the sea | *A player who comes on to replace another
exercise: In maths, which word starts with «sub-» and means take away? | Submarine | Subway | Subscription | *Subtract
exercise: «Coaches notice attitude, and cheering and watching the game keep a sub ready to go on.» What does a sub do to stay ready? | Eats a long sandwich | *Watches, cheers and waits to go on | Swims under the bench | Pays money to the club
test: «Kids grow at very different times, so small at 10 tells little about 16.» What is the prefix in the word «submarine» that means under? | pre- | sup- | *sub- | sun-
test: In the UK, someone says, «Can you sub me a pound until Friday?» What does sub mean here? | A kind of train under the city | A long sandwich | A substitute player | *To lend someone a little money
exam: The prefix «sub-» means under or below. Which word means a train that runs under the city? | Prehistoric | Subtotal, which is a total of all the numbers added up | *Subway | Preview
